{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>יֵשֵׁב</b> [in the phrase] מִן — on the pattern of צו את בני ישראל (Numbers 28:2), with the word אשר missing, like עם לבבכם שלם (I Kings 2:4). And many like it. And so is חסד ואמת מן יצרוהו — with [the word] אשר missing, like: וימן HaShem (Job 32:13)."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 61, :notes {0 "The comment addresses syntactic ellipsis of אשר across three verse examples; the heading phrase 'מן' is Ibn Ezra's abbreviation indicating he is discussing the prefixed min in the lemma. The third example reads מן יצרוהו, i.e. the min is overt in that verse, unlike the first two cases where אשר is elided."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:32:29.897251584Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}